  "SQL": {
    "kernels": "SELECT k.start,k.end,s.value,k.graphId,k.correlationId,r.start,k.streamId FROM CUPTI_ACTIVITY_KIND_KERNEL k JOIN StringIds s ON s.id=k.demangledName LEFT JOIN CUPTI_ACTIVITY_KIND_RUNTIME r ON r.correlationId=k.correlationId ORDER BY k.start",
    "graph_capture_launches": "SELECT r.start,g.graphId,g.streamId FROM CUPTI_ACTIVITY_KIND_RUNTIME r JOIN StringIds s ON s.id=r.nameId JOIN CUPTI_ACTIVITY_KIND_GRAPH_TRACE g ON g.correlationId=r.correlationId WHERE s.value LIKE 'cudaGraphLaunch%' ORDER BY r.start",
    "copies": "SELECT c.start,c.end,c.bytes,c.streamId FROM CUPTI_ACTIVITY_KIND_MEMCPY c WHERE c.copyKind=2 AND c.streamId=14 AND c.bytes IN (56,12368) ORDER BY c.start"
  },
  "independent_method": [
    "Group NODE graph kernels by runtime cudaGraphLaunch correlation and order the launches by host API start; identify D by decode and M by packet kernel, then pair all 60 launch ordinals to GRAPH-capture graph IDs and real streams.",
    "Map frame n using nth F05 and nth D/M launch pair; independently check F02<F05<D launch<M launch<next F05 host ordering, D GPU completion<=mask<=M graph, and M D2H completion<=next-frame begin/input for all30.",
    "Find F03 as all D graph kernels completed before its first producer initialize/finite/aggregate kernel. This independently yields302 engine kernels,3 producer kernels and5 F04 kernels per frame.",
    "Full F06 begins at flow_input and ends after flow_output writes the working gray image. Its actual CUDA kernels are the M-stream kernels in that interval. flow_mask and predict are separate.",
    "Tail for cross-frame statistics is flow_mask plus all9 M graph kernels. Merge each actual activity list, intersect the normalized lists using a two-pointer sweep; bounding envelopes are computed separately.",
    "Exclude zero-based frames0,1; steady frames2..29 yield28 same-frame samples and adjacent pairs n=2..28 yield27 cross-frame samples.",
    "Compare all30 timeline segments against independently reconstructed event bounds, counts, busy intervals and logical streams. Compare30 SVG measured-bar x/width values to those bounds, allowing only3-decimal SVG rounding."
  ],
